      "description": "Log/journal, kept by, Anonymous (5 November - 24 October 1949) on the Ship St. Peter of New Bedford documenting a whaling voyage to the Indian Ocean.  Whaling in western part of Indian Ocean , Mozambique to Seychelles; Seychelles landfalls include much about Madame Davies' Establishment (purportedly respectable); May 1850 mentions toggle iron; cook falls asleep, falls overboard, drowned.\n \n Subjects: Whaling--Massachuetts--New Bedford; Indian Ocean--Description and travel; Logbooks; Voyages and travels; Whalers (Persons); Whales; Whaling masters",
      "artist": "St. Peter (Ship) \n Almy, William H.",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "licenseUrl": "",
      "date": ""
    },
