          "value": "<div class=\"description\">\n<p>Logbook, kept by two keepers, comprised of two voyages. First voyage documents the Montgomery (Ship) of New Haven, mastered by Trowbridge, kept by Jeremiah Townsend III, from 29 January 1784-3 April 1784. Not whaling, pp. 359-399. New Haven to Londonderry, Ireland. MS fair copy made by Thomas R. Trowbridge Jr., 1880s. Second voyage documenst the Neptune (Ship) of New Haven, mastered by Daniel Greene, kept by Ebenezer Townsend, from 1 January 1797-11 July 1799. Sealing voyage, pp. 5-357. South Pacific Ocean, Hawaii, and Canton (China). MS fair copy made by Thomas R. Trowbridge Jr., 1883.\n</p>\n<br>Subjects: Whaling--Connecticut--New haven; Logbooks; Voyages and travels; Whalers (Persons); Whales; Whaling masters</div>",
